<title>USA: Blizzard-hit ranchers merit tax break-US senators.</title>
<headline>Blizzard-hit ranchers merit tax break-US senators.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three U.S. senators filed a bill Thursday to give ranchers an income-tax break if they are forced to liquidate herds due to severe weather, such as the blizzards that have swept the northern Plains.</p>
<p>The bill was filed by Democrats Byron Dorgan of North Dakota and Tom Daschle and Tim Johnson of South Dakota.</p>
<p>One section of the bill would allow livestock producers to defer tax on income from the sale of herds if they buy replacement stock within two years. The other section allows producers who did not re-invest to elect to defer proceeds from sale of livestock to the tax year following the sale.</p>
</text>
